---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chrome from '../components/Chrome.astro';
import SiteFoot from '../components/SiteFoot.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<Base title="About: Yelta Köm and Team" description="Studio No Frame is an exhibition architecture studio in Berlin, led by architect and artist Yelta Köm. Team, approach and the institutions we have worked with.">
  <Chrome here="about" />
  <section class="page">
    <h1>Profile</h1>

    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Studio No Frame designs exhibition architecture for exhibitions of
        contemporary art, architecture and research. The studio is based in
        Berlin and works with curators, artists, institutions, project spaces
        and universities.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work covers exhibition architecture, production, artist
        collaborations, spatial research and curation. Each project starts from
        the curatorial concept and the existing building: the route through the
        rooms, how works are seen and read, and what can be reused or taken
        apart afterwards.
      </p>

      <h2>Institutions and artists</h2>
      <p>
        Haus der Kulturen der Welt, Istanbul Foundation for Culture and Arts
        (İKSV), Istanbul Modern, Museum Ludwig, MAXXI Rome, Pera Museum, SALT,
        La Biennale di Venezia, the Istanbul Biennial, the Istanbul Design
        Biennial and the Timișoara Biennial. Artists we have worked with
        include Abbas Zahedi, Ahmet Öğüt, Amy Lien &amp; Enzo Camacho, Ayşe
        Erkmen, Füsun Onur, Gülsün Karamustafa, Leman Darıcıoğlu, Monira Al
        Qadiri, Raul Walch and Tomás Saraceno.
      </p>

      <h2>Team</h2>
      <p>
        The studio is led by <strong>Yelta Köm</strong> (b. 1986, Istanbul),
        architect and artist. Yelta Köm studied architecture at Yıldız Technical
        University in Istanbul and at the Städelschule in Frankfurt am Main, and
        is a research associate at the Chair of Practices and Politics of
        Representation, Bauhaus-Universität Weimar.
      </p>
      <p>
        The team changes with each exhibition: designers, researchers and
        production managers are brought together for the work at hand.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Current team</strong><br />
        Kubilay Ercelep
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Former team and collaborators</strong><br />
        Ece Aktuğ, Gökalp Alaca, Ali Haydar Ararut, Elif Çak, Selin Doğaner, Bengü Erdem, Pelin Gezer, Nisa Gökgöz, İdil Gökgöz, Deniz İnal, Serap Kaçmaz, Utku Kan, Melisa Karataş, Yesol Kim, Emek Şayan, Elif Tan
      </p>

      <h2>Working with us</h2>
      <p>
        To see the full portfolio or discuss a project,
        {' '}<a href={`${base}/contact`}>get in touch</a>. If you are looking for an
        internship, the details are on the
        {' '}<a href={`${base}/internships`}>internships page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SiteFoot />
</Base>
